<p>Henry L. Dahners was born in Hastings, Minnesota on April 23, 1888 to Hubert and Rosella (Ley) Dahners. He received his education in St. Paul, Minnesota. In 1909 he left St. Paul to join a boyhood friend in Bowbells, ND and to go with him to Calgary, Alberta, Canada. While in Bowbells he met and later married a young school teacher by the name of Alice Kennedy on April 8, 1912. They were the parents to 3 children: Lucile, Gwen and Gregory. They lived in Calgary, Alberta, Canada for four years where he was hired to manage the Home Plate Cigar Store and keep the books for the professional baseball team whose headquarters were in the store.</p>

